Progressive disease activity
These findings strongly suggest long-standing dysregulation of immune signaling pathways.

Recurrent Infection
The development of secondary skin infection indicates simultaneous immune dysfunction.
Importantly, immune dysfunction does not necessarily imply immune deficiency.
Rather, it often reflects impaired immune regulation.
The coexistence of inflammation and infection is characteristic of disrupted Biological Dynamic.

