Structural Integrity of Living Systems
Biointegrity refers to the ability of biological structures to maintain physical integrity, functional coherence, and barrier protection.
Examples include:
Skin barrier integrity
Intestinal barrier integrity
Vascular integrity
Tissue architecture
Extracellular matrix organization
When Biointegrity deteriorates, organisms become increasingly vulnerable to inflammation, infection, fluid loss, and systemic instability.

