Interrupting chronic inflammatory feedback loops.
Tissue Injury Network
Reducing inflammation-induced cellular damage.
By suppressing inflammatory signaling at multiple hierarchical levels, Kerra effectively decreased the biological noise driving disease perpetuation.
11.4 Minoza Module:
Immune Reprogramming and Resolution Network
Whereas Kerra primarily suppresses inflammatory signaling, Minoza serves a complementary role by promoting immune recalibration.
The distinction is important.
Chronic inflammatory diseases frequently arise not merely from excessive inflammation but from failure of inflammatory resolution.
In such conditions, the immune system becomes trapped in a persistent activated state.
Experimental findings suggest that Minoza possesses both anti-inflammatory and immunomodulatory activities, including reduction of inflammatory mediators and modulation of immune signaling pathways. �
