Gut Barrier Network
Gut–Immune Communication Network
Gut–Brain Communication Network
The persistence of these improvements strongly suggests that microbiome recovery represented one of the earliest successful therapeutic responses.
Because the microbiome occupies a central position within the disease network architecture, restoration of microbial ecology likely contributed to downstream improvements throughout the organism.
12.4 Recovery of Immune Regulatory Networks
