This transition represents a fundamental reorganization of biological architecture.

13.9 Restoration of Organismal Homeostasis
Homeostasis is not a static state.
Rather, it is a dynamic process through which biological systems continuously adapt to changing conditions.
The patient demonstrated multiple indicators of improving homeostasis:
improved digestion
